    "body": "fix on mkinney:issue/303-chamfer-deburr-gouge · PR #502 · pinned by edge_break_gate (a_default_2d_chamfer_on_a_finished_brick_posts, a_default_deburr_on_a_finished_brick_posts, a_chamfer_ridden_deeper_than_its_stated_break_still_refuses, a_chamfer_on_an_edge_it_was_not_asked_to_break_still_refuses, the_declared_break_survives_save_and_load), edge_break_credit (sim), deburr::a_vertical_edge_is_skipped_out_loud_never_countersunk · merges when reviewed\n\nFinding: the deburr's deeper gouge columns were not link rapids. They were its rides down the brick's vertical corner edges, which countersank each corner to the window floor (9.80 mm with the defaults). That is a real gouge. The deburr now skips edges steeper than its cone's flank and says so in a path note.",
